C++20 <map>: operator[] insert + access.

Reclassified CORE -> KNOWNBUG by the member-typedef conformance fix
([temp.inst]/1-2, [dcl.typedef]).  Previously this passed only because the
non-conformant *truncated* std::map had its operations havoc'd (symex executed
none of the real container; the property was vacuous).  The fix makes the front
end conformant and symex now executes the REAL std::map / _Rb_tree machinery.

Current layer (2026-07-15): reading back an inserted key (`m[1] == 42`)
mis-evaluates because std::pair's PIECEWISE constructor converts to an
EMPTY body: it is defined out-of-line in <tuple> as a DELEGATING
constructor (`: pair(__first, __second,
_Build_index_tuple<sizeof...(_Args1)>::__type(), ...)`), and the
delegating mem-initializer of an out-of-line two-pack member template is
dropped.  The stored key stays zero / the read-back re-inserts, and
without an unwind bound the tree walk over the resulting nondet-shaped
tree unwinds without terminating.  The upstream pieces of the chain
(new-initializer pack expansion, [temp.inst]/2 member-template body
preservation, [over.match.funcs]/2 object pairing) are fixed and covered
by cpp11_pack_expansion_new_init / cpp11_member_template_object_arg.

Second-tier verification-PERFORMANCE item, not a conformance one; the previous
"pass" was unsound.  Reclassify back to CORE once symex is tractable on the real
container.
See doc/architectural/cpp-class-template-instantiation-plan.md.
